STEP 5  the mechanism, seen directly in the residues
  A node admits branch v iff it lies in ONE class mod A(v).  Powers
  of 2 do not visit those classes uniformly -- they visit the cyclic
  subgroup <2>.  If that is the whole story, the skew must persist
  at every depth for the halting tree and be absent for generic roots.

  --- node residues mod A(0) = 5; branch 0 needs class 1; uniform would be 0.200 ---
